P5 modelled two chart families as a structural guess. The sourcing round
returned FIVE attested ones, and the taxonomy is carried here as a data table
with a per-instance SOURCING TIER, because the person directing this work
reads only Western notation and an unverified claim about a living tradition
is exactly the failure mode this project exists to prevent — getting a
non-Western system wrong would privilege Western notation by default.

10 instances: 9 VERIFIED-OA, 1 EXPERT-WEB, 0 unsourced claims stated as fact.

**THREE of five families chart the interval carrier** (differential /
scale-degree / absolute-position). **TWO do not** — and the two that resist
are not the exotic ones: Western lute and guitar tablature sit in the same
bucket as jianzipu, because instrument-action notations chart the
INSTRUMENT's configuration space with pitch as an OUTPUT. Kepatihan is a
fourth thing again, degree-fixed and pitch-floating, and conflating it with
movable-do would be an error.

Measured: the action->pitch map is total but NOT injective backwards
(preimage histogram {1:10, 2:13, 3:14}) — reproducing the sourced
pitch->tab one-to-many claim. The loss is not spelling; it is WHICH PHYSICAL
ACTION was taken, which the pitch carrier structurally cannot hold.

**F24 is the finding that bounds the whole design.** Jianzipu characters may
omit the left-hand half, meaning the position PERSISTS from the previous
character (VERIFIED-OA). So the symbol->carrier map is not a function of the
symbol: measured, one 6-symbol sequence yields 12 DISTINCT readings across 12
start states. A chart in the atlas sense is a FUNCTION; this is a TRANSDUCER,
(symbol, state) -> (value, state'). The torsor/atlas language reaches three of
the five families and NOT this one, and the spec says so.

Two corrections left visible in the source rather than patched away:
* F24's first probe opened with a position-setting symbol, which overwrote
  the start state on step 1 and reported "identical" for a reason having
  nothing to do with the notation. The corrected probe opens with a HOLD —
  the real case of a fragment entered mid-piece.
* the Seeger prescriptive/descriptive axis is ABANDONED, not used: Seeger
  1958 is verified, but the Carnatic literature inverts the terms, so half
  the field would read the claim backwards. COMPLETE vs SKELETAL, applied
  per dimension, replaces it.

The F24-to-F9 resemblance (statefulness vs associator path-dependence) is
recorded as an OPEN QUESTION and explicitly not resolved: one state is a
convention about ink, the other is an algebra's associator, and a shared
structural name is not object identity.

